  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DataTally",
      "text": "**Official domain: https://datatally.xyz**\n\n**Help AI find the most valuable data.**\n帮助 AI 找到最值钱的数据。\n\n**DataTally records. AI judges.**\n\n*For AI, \"valuable\" means worth the compute — the cost of using data is time and tokens, not money. DataTally helps AI find data worth using.*\n\nDataTally is a [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) plugin that aggregates public usage signals of data assets — downloads, citations, stars — into a single, verifiable profile.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "Data has no intrinsic properties. A byte count says nothing about value. The only real signal of a data asset's value is **how it has been used** — by whom, how often, and with what results. DataTally collects those usage signals from public sources and presents them in one place:"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "| Tool | What it does |\n|------|-------------|\n| `search_assets` | Search data asset profiles by keyword or domain |\n| `get_asset_profile` | Get the full usage profile of one asset: per-source metrics, timeline, citations |\n| `compare_assets` | Compare two assets across dimensions (within the same signal layer) |\n\nEvery metric carries its source and fetch time. Nothing is interpreted. Nothing is ranked. **DataTally records; you judge.**"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "DataTally **never**: computes value, weighs signals, ranks assets, recommends \"which is better\", sells data, or fabricates numbers. The record is DataTally's. The interpretation is the user's.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Signal layers",
      "text": "- **Deep signals** — actual use: downloads, citations, forks, commits\n- **Shallow signals** — interest only: stars, likes (\"bookmarked\" ≠ \"used\")\n\nLayers describe behavior versus interest — **not a strength scale**. Comparisons are only made within the same layer. A star is not a download. Missing provenance is marked explicitly — a single-source asset says so in its profile summary; a missing license surfaces as `null`, never a fabricated default.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires DeepSeek Harness installed (`dsh` on your PATH) and Node.js ≥ 22.19.\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add datatally\ndsh web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From a checkout (development)",
      "text": "```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/DAAMAAO/datatally.git\ncd datatally-plugin\nnpm install\nnpm run typecheck\n\nLoad it into a running dsh for end-to-end testing:\n\n```bash\ndsh web --patch ./cordis.patch.yml"
    },
    {
      "section": "(replace the `name` in cordis.patch.yml with the absolute path to src/index.ts)",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use it",
      "text": "Ask your agent:\n\n> \"Find datasets for sentiment analysis and compare the two most used ones.\"\n\nThe agent will call `search_assets`, then `compare_assets`, and answer with sourced usage data. An actual session transcript:\n\n**User**：帮我找情感分析的数据集，然后对比两个使用最多的\n\n**Agent**（调 `search_assets(\"sentiment\")`）：\n\n> - imdb (stanfordnlp/imdb) | domain: nlp | deep: downloads 195,669 | shallow: likes 725 | fetched_at: 2026-09-08T14:35:50Z | snapshot: v2\n> - glue (nyu-mll/glue) | deep: downloads 826,859 … （共 8 个命中）"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use it",
      "text": "**Agent**（调 `compare_assets(\"nyu-mll/glue\", \"stanfordnlp/imdb\")`）：\n\n> - downloads [deep]: 791,429 vs 197,595 | same_source: true | same_access: true\n> - forks [deep]: 178 vs 0 | same_source: false | same_access: true\n> - likes [shallow]: 741 vs 722 | same_source: true | same_access: true\n> note: cross-source metrics are not directly comparable\n\n**Agent** 的最终回答只陈述记录（引用次数、来源、抓取时间），**不下\"哪个更好\"的结论**——判断留给用户。\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "The plugin ships with defaults; override per row in your profile patch:\n\n| Field | Default | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|---------|\n| `snapshotPath` | `./data/snapshot_v2.json` | Local snapshot file. Relative paths resolve against the process cwd first, then against the package's bundled `data/` seed. |\n| `maxResults` | `20` | Search result cap (the `limit` parameter is clamped to it). |\n| `enableCitationFields` | `true` | Include the `citations` field in profiles. |\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Snapshot format",
      "text": "DataTally reads usage data from a **local, self-owned** JSON file (version 2). Replace the seed by pointing `snapshotPath` at your own file:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": \"2\",\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-09-06T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"assets\": ["
    },
    {
      "section": "Snapshot format",
      "text": "Schema principles: structured from day one · every field has a source · evidence attributes are facts, not interpretations · snapshots are self-owned · machine-readable first. Unknown fields (including the legacy `asset_class`) are rejected loudly; v1 snapshots are rejected with a migration pointer.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "CLI",
      "text": "The same core, in a terminal (the thin-wrapper form over the plugin core):\n\n```bash\ndatatally profile stanfordnlp/imdb\ndatatally search sentiment --domain nlp --limit 5\ndatatally compare HuggingFaceFW/fineweb allenai/c4\ndatatally export nyu-mll/glue      # AI-BOM fact entry: pure facts, no conclusions\ndatatally catalog                  # per-sector distributions (multi-source rate, model-use density)"
    },
    {
      "section": "snapshot location: --snapshot <path> or DATATALLY_SNAPSHOT env",
      "text": "```\n\nThe CLI is **read-side only**: every command reads a snapshot file. Rebuilding a snapshot (the four-source refresh pipeline) is a maintainer operation in the private workspace; the pipeline never ships in this package or the public repository.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```\nsrc/\n├── index.ts              # plugin entry: Config + apply + tool registration\n├── core/                 # pure query logic (no harness deps) + text rendering\n├── tools/                # one defineTool per file: schema + execute + render + UI cards"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "The maintainer's local checkout additionally holds the **private refresh pipeline** (`src/snapshot/fetchers/` and its tests): excluded from this repository by `.gitignore` plus a hard deny-gate in the push script, and never present in npm tarballs (the `files` allowlist has no matching glob)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "- `npm run typecheck` — strict TypeScript, no errors\n- `npm test` — builds, then runs the read-side suite (42 tests) including keyless drive tests through the real `ctx.tools.execute` pipeline\n- Peer packages (`@deepseek-ai/cordis`, `dsh-tools`, `dsh-llm`) are provided by the DeepSeek Harness deployment, exactly like the official dsh tool plugins.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Data provenance",
      "text": "The seed snapshot carries **real public usage data** for **126 open Hugging Face datasets across 9 industry sectors** — core (famous benchmarks + sentiment classics), protein, agri-commodity, auto-sales, aviation, insurance-weather, carbon, power, and logistics — aggregated from up to four public sources (fetched 2026-09-08). Each asset carries an optional `sector` label, searchable like any other field:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Data provenance",
      "text": "| Source | Signals |\n|--------|---------|\n| Hugging Face Hub | downloads, likes, model uses (deep / shallow / deep) |\n| ModelScope | downloads, likes (mirrored datasets, probed by short name) |\n| DataCite | citation counts (when the dataset card carries a DOI) |\n| GitHub | stars (shallow), forks/commits (deep) — only for curated dataset→repo mappings whose repo is the dataset's canonical release home (see `data/curated.json`) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Data provenance",
      "text": "Provenance discipline: every metric carries its `source` + `fetched_at`; `model_uses` is exact below the scan cap and recorded as `model_uses_min` (an honest lower bound) at the cap; single-source assets are marked explicitly (\"single source only — multi-source aggregation not met\"); missing provenance is never fabricated. Hugging Face numbers were fetched through the hf-mirror.com mirror (counts are the mirror's index, which can differ from hf.co's counters); the maintainer-private refresh reads `DATATALLY_HF_BASE` (default https://huggingface.co) to switch channels."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data provenance",
      "text": "**On calibers, stated neutrally**: a platform's own statistics are one caliber among several. Each caliber is recorded separately with its source and fetch time, and a profile that aggregates several calibers is more complete than one that does not — no platform's statistics are attacked or preferred; the record simply states what each caliber shows."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data provenance",
      "text": "The seed snapshot is produced by the maintainer's **private four-source refresh pipeline**. The public package and repository are read-side only: they ship and read snapshots, they never fetch. To get a fresh snapshot, ask the maintainer to run the private pipeline and ship the updated `data/snapshot_v2.json`.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing",
      "text": "Issues and pull requests welcome. Please keep contributions within the stated scope: **recording usage signals, not interpreting them.**"
    }
  ],
